# Units declared by scripts/04-verify-branding.sh.
#
# The old "(53 checks)" summary counted `check` call sites in the source text,
# all of them outside every guard, so it printed 53 whether a check ran or
# self-skipped. That is the shape that let a relocated src/config/Config.zig
# print a full green run out of a shipping gate.
#
# guarded-subjects replaces it with the question that actually matters: did the
# checks have subjects to check? 58 blocks sit behind `if [ -f "..." ]`, and a
# collapsed subject set now fails rather than reading as clean.

upstream-path-manifest
guarded-subjects
